1
00:00:00,549 --> 00:00:02,134
[people cheering]

2
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:07,931
[Chinatsu] <i>Okay.</i>

3
00:00:08,015 --> 00:00:09,474
EIMEI

4
00:00:09,558 --> 00:00:10,934
<i>If he wins, I'll ask him...</i>

5
00:00:12,019 --> 00:00:13,395
<i>to the aquarium.</i>

6
00:00:16,106 --> 00:00:18,108
[opening theme song playing]

7
00:00:19,192 --> 00:00:22,446
BLUE BOX

8
00:01:38,647 --> 00:01:44,945
BLUE BOX

9
00:01:45,612 --> 00:01:47,948
EPISODE 5
AQUARIUM

10
00:01:48,031 --> 00:01:50,033
[both grunting]

11
00:01:51,284 --> 00:01:52,160
[Kishi] <i>One point.</i>

12
00:01:53,954 --> 00:01:56,206
<i>I can't afford to make any mistakes.</i>

13
00:01:57,165 --> 00:01:58,750
<i>If I don't win this point...</i>

14
00:02:02,546 --> 00:02:03,588
[grunts]

15
00:02:05,298 --> 00:02:06,216
[gasps]

16
00:02:08,802 --> 00:02:09,719
[Kishi groans]

17
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:14,266
[referee] In! Game!

18
00:02:14,808 --> 00:02:16,518
- [crowd cheering]
- [pants]

19
00:02:16,601 --> 00:02:17,769
[Taiki] <i>That was close.</i>

20
00:02:17,853 --> 00:02:20,730
<i>If he'd gone for a push shot,
I wouldn't have made it.</i>

21
00:02:20,814 --> 00:02:22,149
SHIMOTOMI

22
00:02:22,232 --> 00:02:24,276
[pants] Huh?

23
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,989
- Rematch?
- You got it.

24
00:02:29,698 --> 00:02:32,951
Next time that we practice,
I'll come to Eimei.

25
00:02:33,034 --> 00:02:34,369
Yeah, please do.

26
00:02:34,452 --> 00:02:35,704
Oh, I'll be there!

27
00:02:36,913 --> 00:02:39,583
Make sure to check
when girls' basketball's practicing!

28
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:41,710
Come on! [grunts]

29
00:02:41,793 --> 00:02:44,421
- He's leaving with his head held high.
- You think so?

30
00:02:44,504 --> 00:02:47,799
He's not one to show it,
but I bet he's feeling the loss.

31
00:02:50,010 --> 00:02:52,554
{\an8}[Nishida] It's really too bad, Taiki.

32
00:02:52,637 --> 00:02:54,264
[laughs]

33
00:02:54,347 --> 00:02:56,766
If only you'd managed
to beat The Great Nishida,

34
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:58,059
you could've won it all.

35
00:02:58,143 --> 00:03:00,645
There's still the prefectural qualifiers,

36
00:03:00,729 --> 00:03:03,189
don't giveth up the fight,
young squire! [laughs]

37
00:03:03,273 --> 00:03:04,316
Adieu!

38
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:06,526
Kyo,

39
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:09,112
I think Nishida is just not my cup of tea.

40
00:03:09,195 --> 00:03:10,906
Well, regardless of how he acts,

41
00:03:10,989 --> 00:03:13,575
he's still one
of the second-years' top players.

42
00:03:14,242 --> 00:03:16,119
- [Hina] Oh, hey, Two-ki!
- Hm?

43
00:03:16,202 --> 00:03:18,330
Well, you got second, so you're Two-ki!

44
00:03:18,413 --> 00:03:20,790
Don't start giving me nicknames.

45
00:03:20,874 --> 00:03:23,126
Hopefully, next time, you'll be One-ki!

46
00:03:23,209 --> 00:03:24,586
That isn't any better!

47
00:03:24,669 --> 00:03:26,630
[Hina] I heard all about it!

48
00:03:26,713 --> 00:03:30,091
Sounds like you put up quite the fight,
especially for a first-year!

49
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:33,345
And that's pretty good! For you, anyway.

50
00:03:33,970 --> 00:03:36,139
Why are you being such a butt?

51
00:03:36,223 --> 00:03:38,099
You have a shot at nationals, right?

52
00:03:38,183 --> 00:03:39,476
[Taiki] Exactly.

53
00:03:39,559 --> 00:03:42,020
- So leading up to that, I have to...
- [phone chimes]

54
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,856
[screams]

55
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,358
WANNA GO TO THE AQUARIUM TOMORROW?

56
00:03:46,441 --> 00:03:48,360
IT'S OKAY IF YOU'RE TOO TIRED!

57
00:03:48,443 --> 00:03:51,112
[exclaims, chokes]

58
00:03:54,866 --> 00:03:55,867
[Kyo] Breathe, dude.

59
00:03:55,951 --> 00:03:58,954
Taiki, when did the two of you
get to be so close?

60
00:03:59,037 --> 00:04:00,121
[Taiki] Huh?

61
00:04:00,205 --> 00:04:02,207
Oh. Well... We are...

62
00:04:03,124 --> 00:04:04,876
- [Kyo] I asked her to do it.
- [Hina] Huh?

63
00:04:05,669 --> 00:04:08,505
Chinatsu happened to be at the gym,
and was watching the match.

64
00:04:08,588 --> 00:04:09,881
[Taiki] For real?

65
00:04:10,548 --> 00:04:11,758
A deal was struck that

66
00:04:11,841 --> 00:04:15,136
if your opponent won,
then he would get introduced to Chinatsu.

67
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:18,932
And I said, if you won,
she should take you out somewhere.

68
00:04:19,015 --> 00:04:19,975
[gasps softly]

69
00:04:21,226 --> 00:04:23,270
It'll be your very first date!

70
00:04:23,353 --> 00:04:24,646
[Taiki] Da...

71
00:04:24,729 --> 00:04:26,064
[Hina] Well done!

72
00:04:26,147 --> 00:04:27,565
Ah, no way.

73
00:04:27,649 --> 00:04:30,652
I'm sure she only asked me
'cause Kyo made her!

74
00:04:30,735 --> 00:04:32,696
You wouldn't go to the aquarium
with someone

75
00:04:32,779 --> 00:04:34,990
just because of something like that.

76
00:04:35,073 --> 00:04:36,366
- [Niina] Hina!
- Oh.

77
00:04:39,035 --> 00:04:40,996
[Hina] This'll be
your first date ever Taiki,

78
00:04:41,663 --> 00:04:43,748
so you better make sure
you're wearing clean clothes!

79
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:45,875
That was only...

80
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:47,210
You got this!

81
00:04:48,753 --> 00:04:51,631
[Hina] <i>Would you look at that.
He didn't waste any time.</i>

82
00:04:51,715 --> 00:04:53,967
<i>- Good for him! Good for him!</i>
- Hm?

83
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:54,968
Huh?

84
00:04:55,051 --> 00:04:57,762
- Are you upset about something?
- What?

85
00:05:01,808 --> 00:05:03,143
Am I?

86
00:05:03,226 --> 00:05:05,353
I might've put on half a kilo?

87
00:05:05,437 --> 00:05:07,397
[Niina] Yeah, no wonder you're pissed.

88
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:12,819
[grunting]

89
00:05:20,076 --> 00:05:21,911
<i>I can't go inside yet!</i>

90
00:05:22,495 --> 00:05:23,747
<i>Oh, I know!</i>

91
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:27,709
<i>Chinatsu is just doing something nice
for me because we live together.</i>

92
00:05:27,792 --> 00:05:30,628
<i>There's absolutely no deeper meaning
to be found here!</i>

93
00:05:30,712 --> 00:05:32,047
[grunts]

94
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:33,631
Huh.

95
00:05:34,799 --> 00:05:38,053
- Quit messing around and get inside.
- Got it.

96
00:05:38,136 --> 00:05:40,013
[man on TV] <i>Do you know
any good restaurants?</i>

97
00:05:40,096 --> 00:05:43,308
Huh? Where is Chinatsu?

98
00:05:43,391 --> 00:05:45,060
She went up to her room already.

99
00:05:45,143 --> 00:05:46,561
She did?

100
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:50,398
<i>I was hoping to see her, but I guess not.</i>

101
00:05:51,149 --> 00:05:53,068
TAIKI

102
00:05:53,151 --> 00:05:54,694
FIELD GUIDE TO CREATURES
OCEANS

103
00:05:54,778 --> 00:05:57,822
{\an8}Porcupine fish have 350 to 400 spines.

104
00:05:58,782 --> 00:06:02,577
{\an8}A jellyfish's body
is made up of 95% water.

105
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,037
[groans]

106
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,538
<i>Kyo, that helpful jerk!</i>

107
00:06:05,622 --> 00:06:09,209
<i>Why didn't he suggest she take me out
in a month, so I can prepare?</i>

108
00:06:09,292 --> 00:06:10,335
[amusing music playing]

109
00:06:10,418 --> 00:06:11,294
{\an8}SPRING STYLING

110
00:06:11,377 --> 00:06:14,923
{\an8}<i>And I have absolutely no idea
what I'm supposed to wear.</i>

111
00:06:17,092 --> 00:06:20,345
<i>I wonder what Chinatsu's going to wear.</i>

112
00:06:21,346 --> 00:06:23,473
{\an8}<i>I'd love to see her in a dress.</i>

113
00:06:24,224 --> 00:06:26,434
{\an8}<i>Chinatsu in a dress.</i>

114
00:06:27,185 --> 00:06:29,521
<i>No! No expectations.</i>

115
00:06:30,021 --> 00:06:31,606
<i>This is not a date.</i>

116
00:06:32,398 --> 00:06:36,152
<i>This is more like...
like a family outing or something.</i>

117
00:06:36,236 --> 00:06:38,029
- [thudding]
- [gasps]

118
00:06:39,614 --> 00:06:40,615
Huh?

119
00:06:40,698 --> 00:06:41,574
CHINATSU

120
00:06:41,658 --> 00:06:44,369
<i>She's... still awake.</i>

121
00:06:44,911 --> 00:06:47,413
[heart beating]

122
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:52,627
<i>Oh, man.</i>

123
00:06:54,629 --> 00:06:57,006
<i>This is getting my hopes up too high.</i>

124
00:07:00,176 --> 00:07:01,719
<i>But I can't help it.</i>

125
00:07:05,723 --> 00:07:07,642
- [birds chirping]
- [alarm beeping]

126
00:07:08,935 --> 00:07:10,145
[alarm stops]

127
00:07:10,812 --> 00:07:11,771
[groans]

128
00:07:14,482 --> 00:07:16,401
SATURDAY

129
00:07:19,404 --> 00:07:20,488
I overslept!

130
00:07:21,948 --> 00:07:23,074
I'm leaving!

131
00:07:25,577 --> 00:07:27,412
<i>Crap, and on a day like today.</i>

132
00:07:27,495 --> 00:07:30,915
<i>How can I wake up early
every day, except today?</i>

133
00:07:33,001 --> 00:07:34,461
[pants]

134
00:07:36,713 --> 00:07:39,048
<i>Calm down. I need to calm down.</i>

135
00:07:41,468 --> 00:07:42,927
<i>This is not a date.</i>

136
00:07:44,512 --> 00:07:45,680
Are you okay?

137
00:07:46,264 --> 00:07:47,307
[exclaims]

138
00:07:53,605 --> 00:07:55,815
[Taiki] Thank you for asking.

139
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,571
- Is something wrong?
- Huh? No.

140
00:08:05,992 --> 00:08:07,702
[Taiki] <i>She's wearing a dress.</i>

141
00:08:07,785 --> 00:08:09,579
[happy guitar music playing]

142
00:08:18,338 --> 00:08:20,089
Hey, Taiki, this way!

143
00:08:20,173 --> 00:08:23,968
- [Taiki grunts]
- Fishies, fishies, fishies! Yay!

144
00:08:27,013 --> 00:08:30,016
[Taiki] <i>It seems like
she's more cheerful than usual.</i>

145
00:08:30,725 --> 00:08:32,852
<i>I haven't seen her like this before.</i>

146
00:08:33,937 --> 00:08:36,898
<i>I kept telling myself
not to expect anything,</i>

147
00:08:36,981 --> 00:08:40,527
<i>but maybe it's okay
to think of this as a date.</i>

148
00:08:45,323 --> 00:08:46,282
So cute!

149
00:08:46,366 --> 00:08:47,617
[Taiki] <i>Yes, you are!</i>

150
00:08:51,204 --> 00:08:52,372
<i>I do wonder...</i>

151
00:08:53,748 --> 00:08:56,626
<i>what she really thinks
about us being out together.</i>

152
00:08:57,460 --> 00:09:00,505
Oh, I just wanted to go
to the aquarium, that's all!

153
00:09:01,214 --> 00:09:02,549
[Taiki] <i>Very possible.</i>

154
00:09:03,883 --> 00:09:07,095
I can't believe you made me
a prize to be won in a bet.

155
00:09:07,178 --> 00:09:08,471
You'll pay for that.

156
00:09:09,472 --> 00:09:12,392
[Taiki] <i>I don't think she'd say that,
but she wouldn't be wrong.</i>

157
00:09:13,309 --> 00:09:14,811
Well, so, what do you think?

158
00:09:15,353 --> 00:09:16,396
[Chinatsu] Taiki!

159
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,648
[camera clicks]

160
00:09:19,732 --> 00:09:21,651
- Huh?
- Looks great.

161
00:09:21,734 --> 00:09:23,903
[Taiki grunts] Why'd you take
a picture of me?

162
00:09:24,487 --> 00:09:25,905
[Chinatsu] For the memories!

163
00:09:25,989 --> 00:09:27,365
[Taiki] Please delete it.

164
00:09:27,991 --> 00:09:29,701
Not gonna happen.

165
00:09:29,784 --> 00:09:32,161
We going to need something
to remember this day by!

166
00:09:33,079 --> 00:09:34,205
[exclaims]

167
00:09:43,423 --> 00:09:45,049
[Taiki] <i>I wish that was me.</i>

168
00:09:47,635 --> 00:09:51,973
<i>If today's just about the aquarium
for her, I'll never recover.</i>

169
00:09:56,144 --> 00:09:57,687
[both gasp]

170
00:09:58,646 --> 00:10:01,274
[Chinatsu] They're so plump and cute...

171
00:10:01,357 --> 00:10:02,692
[Taiki] Plump?

172
00:10:02,775 --> 00:10:04,777
[Chinatsu] I just wanna squish one.

173
00:10:06,487 --> 00:10:08,573
[Taiki] I wonder
if they're cool to the touch.

174
00:10:14,454 --> 00:10:16,539
[grunts] <i>Don't look directly at her!</i>

175
00:10:17,749 --> 00:10:20,084
Mom, look, over here!

176
00:10:20,168 --> 00:10:21,586
[woman] Masaki, watch out!

177
00:10:27,425 --> 00:10:29,052
Excuse me.

178
00:10:29,135 --> 00:10:30,845
- I'm sorry.
- Oh.

179
00:10:32,263 --> 00:10:33,348
It's all right.

180
00:10:34,098 --> 00:10:35,516
See you!

181
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,019
[Taiki] <i>I'd love to
come back here as a couple.</i>

182
00:10:39,145 --> 00:10:42,315
<i>But I'm not ready
to tell her how I feel yet.</i>

183
00:10:44,067 --> 00:10:46,611
<i>I've got a long way to go till nationals.</i>

184
00:10:46,694 --> 00:10:49,364
<i>And confessing your love
to your housemate?</i>

185
00:10:50,073 --> 00:10:52,867
<i>It could make things
uncomfortable at home.</i>

186
00:10:57,789 --> 00:10:59,374
We should be getting back, huh?

187
00:11:00,958 --> 00:11:02,585
Uh. Hold on!

188
00:11:04,796 --> 00:11:06,923
<i>Why is she always grabbing me?</i>

189
00:11:08,132 --> 00:11:10,385
- Oh. What's up?
- Sorry.

190
00:11:12,345 --> 00:11:13,388
The truth is,

191
00:11:14,472 --> 00:11:17,433
there's something
I wanted to talk to you about today.

192
00:11:17,517 --> 00:11:18,393
Huh?

193
00:11:19,769 --> 00:11:21,396
<i>In this setting?</i>

194
00:11:22,563 --> 00:11:24,148
<i>Right here, right now?</i>

195
00:11:26,067 --> 00:11:27,110
<i>Could she...</i>

196
00:11:28,736 --> 00:11:29,737
What is it?

197
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:33,366
<i>Does she feel the same...</i>

198
00:11:34,617 --> 00:11:35,910
Taiki it's just...

199
00:11:37,870 --> 00:11:38,913
I'm sorry.

200
00:11:40,456 --> 00:11:41,416
[Taiki] Uh...

201
00:11:42,041 --> 00:11:44,293
Um, sorry about?

202
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:47,255
[Chinatsu] The other day.

203
00:11:47,338 --> 00:11:50,133
I said you still have next year
and the year after that.

204
00:11:50,758 --> 00:11:51,801
Wha...

205
00:11:54,011 --> 00:11:55,680
Uh... Oh!

206
00:11:56,222 --> 00:11:57,432
You're sorry for that?

207
00:11:58,516 --> 00:12:01,394
I said it knowing how hard
you've been working lately.

208
00:12:02,437 --> 00:12:04,897
That wasn't
a very thoughtful thing to say.

209
00:12:06,274 --> 00:12:07,442
[Taiki] <i>Of course.</i>

210
00:12:08,025 --> 00:12:11,446
<i>She doesn't know that
I overheard her the other day.</i>

211
00:12:13,656 --> 00:12:16,200
[Chinatsu] <i>And we didn't have
a chance to talk after.</i>

212
00:12:16,909 --> 00:12:20,538
But, I don't want to continue
living together with you, just...

213
00:12:20,621 --> 00:12:23,708
letting things fester,
and never talking about them.

214
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:27,837
So I wanted to apologize to you today.

215
00:12:30,715 --> 00:12:31,841
[sighs]

216
00:12:32,758 --> 00:12:34,886
[Taiki] <i>So that's what this was about.</i>

217
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:40,391
<i>I can't believe I even thought
this might be a date.</i>

218
00:12:42,226 --> 00:12:47,148
<i>So this was all to reward me,
and apologize to me then?</i>

219
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:50,276
<i>She didn't need to apologize.</i>

220
00:12:50,902 --> 00:12:53,154
<i>It actually lit a fire under me.</i>

221
00:12:55,198 --> 00:12:58,409
Chinatsu, I think
you may have overthought it.

222
00:12:58,493 --> 00:12:59,452
[gasps softly]

223
00:13:00,453 --> 00:13:03,998
[chuckles] I don't tend
to hold onto things like that.

224
00:13:04,081 --> 00:13:07,001
And I think that you have
a really valid perspective.

225
00:13:08,419 --> 00:13:10,796
I'm honestly a little bit surprised

226
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:14,759
that you've been worrying yourself
about this for the last week.

227
00:13:17,595 --> 00:13:18,763
<i>Then again...</i>

228
00:13:19,597 --> 00:13:23,893
<i>it makes sense to feel that anxious
while living in a stranger's home.</i>

229
00:13:27,522 --> 00:13:28,981
<i>Let's see...</i>

230
00:13:29,065 --> 00:13:30,650
<i>- Oh, there it is.</i>
- [phone chimes]

231
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:31,817
[Chinatsu exclaims]

232
00:13:35,363 --> 00:13:37,532
MR. CAPE
DOWNLOAD

233
00:13:38,115 --> 00:13:41,244
If you ever feel uncomfortable
living at our house,

234
00:13:41,327 --> 00:13:43,579
- or if you wanna tell me something...
- [phone chimes]

235
00:13:44,121 --> 00:13:45,039
HEY! HEY!

236
00:13:45,122 --> 00:13:46,624
...just send me this sticker.

237
00:13:47,416 --> 00:13:49,043
That'll be the signal.

238
00:13:50,086 --> 00:13:51,546
[chuckles] When I get it,

239
00:13:52,296 --> 00:13:53,923
I'll come and listen to you.

240
00:13:56,884 --> 00:13:58,302
CHINATSU KANO
HEY, HEY

241
00:13:59,011 --> 00:14:02,932
[gasping]

242
00:14:03,015 --> 00:14:04,308
Wait, what is it?

243
00:14:09,605 --> 00:14:10,731
[Taiki gasps softly]

244
00:14:13,985 --> 00:14:15,736
Do you wanna tell me something?

245
00:14:16,362 --> 00:14:17,280
[Chinatsu] Hmm...

246
00:14:17,989 --> 00:14:19,323
Yes, I do.

247
00:14:25,288 --> 00:14:27,957
Taiki Inomata. You're a good housemate.

248
00:14:29,292 --> 00:14:30,835
[Taiki] <i>A good housemate?</i>

249
00:14:32,211 --> 00:14:33,337
[groans]

250
00:14:35,464 --> 00:14:36,507
<i>For now...</i>

251
00:14:37,091 --> 00:14:38,426
<i>I guess that'll do.</i>

252
00:14:41,596 --> 00:14:43,180
[feel-good music playing]

253
00:14:48,811 --> 00:14:50,438
[Kyo] You're chowin' down.

254
00:14:51,397 --> 00:14:53,900
I'm a guy who's trying
to make it to nationals.

255
00:14:53,983 --> 00:14:55,776
[gulps, munching voraciously]

256
00:14:56,986 --> 00:15:00,197
Something's telling me you had
a good time at the aquarium, huh?

257
00:15:01,157 --> 00:15:02,325
[exclaims]

258
00:15:05,536 --> 00:15:06,662
[Taiki] It was fun.

259
00:15:08,164 --> 00:15:09,832
Thanks for doing that.

260
00:15:09,916 --> 00:15:10,958
No prob.

261
00:15:13,044 --> 00:15:14,962
I've been thinking about this a while.

262
00:15:15,046 --> 00:15:15,963
[Taiki] Hm?

263
00:15:16,047 --> 00:15:19,216
I understand why you can't be
the one to instigate things...

264
00:15:19,926 --> 00:15:22,303
but what would you do if Chinatsu...

265
00:15:22,386 --> 00:15:23,471
liked you?

266
00:15:23,554 --> 00:15:26,933
[exclaims] Wha... Me? Huh?

267
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,226
[Kyo] It's a possibility.

268
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:32,021
That... is... not... I... Oh...

269
00:15:34,398 --> 00:15:35,983
I didn't know that.

270
00:15:36,859 --> 00:15:37,735
[gasps softly]

271
00:15:37,818 --> 00:15:38,986
[gasps]

272
00:15:39,612 --> 00:15:40,488
[giggles]

273
00:15:41,572 --> 00:15:42,490
[exclaims]

274
00:15:47,787 --> 00:15:50,706
If it's a possibility,
I would love to date her.

275
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:52,249
Yeah, I got that, dude.

276
00:15:54,043 --> 00:15:55,503
[Hina] Hey, Smiley Face.

277
00:15:55,586 --> 00:15:58,005
You gotta resubmit this.

278
00:15:58,089 --> 00:15:59,715
Hina.

279
00:15:59,799 --> 00:16:01,384
You can't live in la-la land.

280
00:16:01,467 --> 00:16:03,511
Check things before you turn 'em in.

281
00:16:04,595 --> 00:16:07,181
And you were grinning
like a dork through the whole class.

282
00:16:09,225 --> 00:16:10,601
I was not.

283
00:16:11,644 --> 00:16:12,645
[Hina groans]

284
00:16:14,230 --> 00:16:16,649
That's the face, right there!
The one you're doing now!

285
00:16:16,732 --> 00:16:17,817
[Taiki] Quit it!

286
00:16:18,442 --> 00:16:20,152
[Hina] That looks of yours bothers me.

287
00:16:21,112 --> 00:16:24,573
Ah, quit it already.
It's gonna get all crinkled!

288
00:16:24,657 --> 00:16:27,410
- [Hina] It's not mine, I don't care.
- Hey!

289
00:16:28,202 --> 00:16:30,746
You really do need
to come back to earth, though.

290
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:32,873
Qualifiers are around the corner.

291
00:16:32,957 --> 00:16:34,166
I know that!

292
00:16:34,250 --> 00:16:35,501
The qualifiers...

293
00:16:36,085 --> 00:16:38,879
will have lots of people
who won regional preliminaries.

294
00:16:39,422 --> 00:16:40,923
I gotta stay focused.

295
00:16:42,425 --> 00:16:43,801
Thanks for the food.

296
00:16:45,511 --> 00:16:47,805
Which school is strongest in badminton?

297
00:16:47,888 --> 00:16:50,850
Sajikawa. They've got
the best badminton team around.

298
00:16:51,517 --> 00:16:52,560
SAJIKAWA

299
00:16:52,643 --> 00:16:55,312
<i>They took it all at nationals last year.</i>

300
00:16:55,396 --> 00:16:58,190
<i>They're beyond prefectures,
they're national-level.</i>

301
00:16:58,816 --> 00:17:02,945
If we don't manage to beat Sajikawa,
we have no chance at nationals.

302
00:17:04,655 --> 00:17:07,074
So then, go and get creamed!

303
00:17:07,867 --> 00:17:09,827
[Taiki] <i>It's a given that I'll lose?</i>

304
00:17:11,287 --> 00:17:13,831
And what's going on with you, Hina?

305
00:17:14,498 --> 00:17:15,958
You have qualifiers, too.

306
00:17:17,001 --> 00:17:19,962
[chuckles] Look at who
you're worrying about.

307
00:17:20,588 --> 00:17:22,673
I'm the great Hina Chono.

308
00:17:23,382 --> 00:17:25,342
"Easy Breezy's" my middle name!

309
00:17:25,968 --> 00:17:27,219
This is when it starts...

310
00:17:27,303 --> 00:17:28,637
- Miss Chono!
- Huh?

311
00:17:29,305 --> 00:17:32,016
[Taiki]
<i>That's the rhythmic gymnastics advisor.</i>

312
00:17:32,099 --> 00:17:33,225
[coach] Splendid timing!

313
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:36,812
This is Shibata from the local newspaper.

314
00:17:36,896 --> 00:17:39,565
As one of the top athletes
going to nationals,

315
00:17:39,648 --> 00:17:41,025
I'd love an interview.

316
00:17:41,108 --> 00:17:42,526
It would be my pleasure.

317
00:17:43,652 --> 00:17:44,612
[chuckles smugly]

318
00:17:45,196 --> 00:17:47,490
[Taiki] <i>Ten points for the smug face.</i>

319
00:17:47,573 --> 00:17:48,699
OPINION BOX

320
00:17:48,783 --> 00:17:50,910
[Shibata] I actually
saw you compete last year.

321
00:17:50,993 --> 00:17:52,244
[Hina] Oh, really, you did?

322
00:17:53,037 --> 00:17:55,456
[Taiki] You know, It feels pretty weird.

323
00:17:55,539 --> 00:17:56,499
[Kyo] Hm?

324
00:17:56,582 --> 00:18:00,211
Well, seeing Sajikawa compete,

325
00:18:00,294 --> 00:18:02,713
it's impossible
not to be impressed by them, right?

326
00:18:02,797 --> 00:18:03,756
Yeah.

327
00:18:04,673 --> 00:18:08,385
[Taiki] Hina's one of those people
you get impressed by at tournaments.

328
00:18:09,136 --> 00:18:11,097
But she's just a normal kid.

329
00:18:11,722 --> 00:18:12,765
[Kyo] Of course she is.

330
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:16,018
Yes, exactly right.

331
00:18:19,313 --> 00:18:20,981
[Kyo] She's just a normal kid.

332
00:18:23,651 --> 00:18:25,528
USHINUMA OSTEOPATHIC CLINIC

333
00:18:25,611 --> 00:18:28,531
Whoa, I can move so much better.

334
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,866
[doctor] Make sure you keep stretching.

335
00:18:31,367 --> 00:18:32,785
[Hina] Thank you, Doctor!

336
00:18:35,162 --> 00:18:36,038
Huh?

337
00:18:37,123 --> 00:18:38,040
[gasps softly]

338
00:18:38,124 --> 00:18:39,208
Good evening.

339
00:18:39,875 --> 00:18:41,043
Good evening.

340
00:18:42,002 --> 00:18:44,588
[receptionist] Miss Kano,
your bill is 27.50.

341
00:18:44,672 --> 00:18:45,756
All right.

342
00:18:46,465 --> 00:18:49,051
[Hina] <i>I didn't know
Chinatsu came to this clinic!</i>

343
00:18:49,969 --> 00:18:51,470
<i>I'll have to tell Taiki.</i>

344
00:18:55,391 --> 00:18:56,475
[gasps]

345
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:01,605
Oh Hina, do you, uh... do treatment here?

346
00:19:01,689 --> 00:19:03,858
[Hina] Uh, it's just for upkeep!

347
00:19:05,276 --> 00:19:06,861
Injuries are scary, huh?

348
00:19:08,779 --> 00:19:10,823
[Hina] <i>I think he has a chance with her.</i>

349
00:19:11,866 --> 00:19:12,825
<i>Hm.</i>

350
00:19:13,409 --> 00:19:14,785
Come to think of it,

351
00:19:14,869 --> 00:19:17,746
do you know Taiki
sprained his ankle in middle school?

352
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:18,831
He did?

353
00:19:18,914 --> 00:19:21,542
Uh-huh. It was on a school camping trip.

354
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:23,586
We were climbing up a mountain.

355
00:19:24,712 --> 00:19:28,841
<i>I slipped, and was about to fall,
but Taiki caught me.</i>

356
00:19:29,758 --> 00:19:32,344
<i>He was the one who ended up getting hurt.</i>

357
00:19:32,428 --> 00:19:35,598
<i>He had to sit out at practice
for almost an entire week.</i>

358
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:39,101
Seeing all that, I yelled at him a little.

359
00:19:39,185 --> 00:19:42,188
[sighs] To know that someone
got injured because of me,

360
00:19:42,271 --> 00:19:46,108
and had to sit out of their club practices
made me feel like crap.

361
00:19:46,192 --> 00:19:47,109
But then he said...

362
00:19:48,527 --> 00:19:50,988
It's my fault
that my reflexes aren't better.

363
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:53,365
Now I have something to work on.

364
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:58,621
He really is a hopeless badminton nerd,
don't ya think, Chinatsu?

365
00:19:59,455 --> 00:20:00,706
[exclaims softly]

366
00:20:03,459 --> 00:20:05,961
But he's got good qualities!

367
00:20:06,045 --> 00:20:08,380
He'll sacrifice himself
for the sake of others!

368
00:20:09,465 --> 00:20:12,426
<i>How about that, Taiki?
I raised your stock with her!</i>

369
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,888
Hina, do you...

370
00:20:15,971 --> 00:20:17,181
Do I...

371
00:20:17,264 --> 00:20:18,265
Oh.

372
00:20:18,349 --> 00:20:19,266
Um...

373
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:20,392
No, nothing.

374
00:20:21,143 --> 00:20:24,230
[receptionist] Miss Chono,
your total is also 27.50.

375
00:20:24,313 --> 00:20:25,397
[Hina] Okay!

376
00:20:25,981 --> 00:20:26,899
[unzipping]

377
00:20:26,982 --> 00:20:28,901
[rain pattering]

378
00:20:29,485 --> 00:20:31,820
Oh, shoot. Forgot my umbrella.

379
00:20:32,529 --> 00:20:34,490
- You can use this one if you want.
- Huh?

380
00:20:35,282 --> 00:20:36,492
But what about you?

381
00:20:36,575 --> 00:20:39,161
Oh, I realized I already had
a foldable one in here.

382
00:20:39,995 --> 00:20:41,163
{\an8}[opens umbrella]

383
00:20:42,957 --> 00:20:44,625
All right, get home safe then.

384
00:20:45,251 --> 00:20:47,086
Thanks so much, Chinatsu.

385
00:20:50,172 --> 00:20:51,173
Hm.

386
00:20:51,799 --> 00:20:53,175
<i>She's so prepared.</i>

387
00:20:54,718 --> 00:20:57,554
<i>She's kind, and cute, and good at sports.</i>

388
00:20:59,682 --> 00:21:02,268
<i>I kinda hope she has some weird fetish.</i>

389
00:21:03,394 --> 00:21:04,687
- Miss Kano!
- Hm?

390
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,230
Did she leave already?

391
00:21:06,730 --> 00:21:08,148
Something the matter, ma'am?

392
00:21:08,232 --> 00:21:09,692
She left her phone behind.

393
00:21:10,484 --> 00:21:12,111
I can get it to her.

394
00:21:16,949 --> 00:21:20,536
She lent me her umbrella after all.
It's the least I can do.

395
00:21:22,830 --> 00:21:23,706
<i>Oh!</i>

396
00:21:23,789 --> 00:21:24,957
<i>Found her!</i>

397
00:21:33,173 --> 00:21:34,383
[gasps]

398
00:21:35,676 --> 00:21:38,387
INOMATA

399
00:21:41,765 --> 00:21:43,892
- Welcome back.
- You going somewhere?

400
00:21:44,601 --> 00:21:46,895
The store, I thought, but... Mm.

401
00:21:47,604 --> 00:21:48,939
I guess I won't go, then.

402
00:21:49,565 --> 00:21:51,400
I would've gone on my way back
if you'd asked.

403
00:21:57,948 --> 00:21:59,158
[breath shudders]

404
00:22:03,704 --> 00:22:04,913
[rain falling heavily]

405
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
